WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.000
-Our first guest tonight

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.300
is an Emmy-nominated
writer and comedian

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.200
you know best from his work
on "Saturday Night Live."

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.000
The second season of his show,
"That Damn Michael Che,"

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.367
is out now on HBO Max.

00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:10.467
Let's take a look.

00:00:10.467 --> 00:00:12.133
-Kim, why don't you tell me

00:00:12.133 --> 00:00:14.467
why you think our relationship
didn't work out?

00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:15.734
-'Cause you had a girlfriend.

00:00:15.734 --> 00:00:18.434
-But what could I have done
differently?

00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:20.200
-You could have told me
you had a girlfriend.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.067
-That's right.
-Alright, alright.

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:23.801
Now, what do you think you could
have done differently?

00:00:23.801 --> 00:00:25.100
-[Bleep]
What you just say to me?

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.501
-Be honest.

00:00:26.501 --> 00:00:29.167
-You know, when we broke up,
he tried to date my sister.

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:31.234
-Wow.
-Well, I didn't know.

00:00:31.234 --> 00:00:33.767
-Yes, you did. Don't lie.
-You didn't let me finish.

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:36.000
I didn't know that
that mattered.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.133
-Huh.
-You're disgusting.

00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:39.501
-He dumped me on Juneteenth.
-Really?

00:00:39.501 --> 00:00:42.100
-I didn't even know that was a
[bleep] holiday until last year.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.534
-Shame on you.

00:00:43.534 --> 00:00:46.334
-Please welcome back to the
show, Michael Che, everybody!

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:48.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:48.634 --> 00:00:55.667
♪♪

00:00:55.667 --> 00:01:03.033
♪♪

00:01:03.033 --> 00:01:06.234
-Welcome back.
-Oh, man, this is awesome.

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:08.367
Hi, Fred.

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:09.534
-Hi.

00:01:09.534 --> 00:01:11.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.300
-It is -- It is very kind of you
to come back into the building,

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:14.868
post-the "SNL" season,

00:01:14.868 --> 00:01:17.033
because obviously you spend
a lot of intense months here,

00:01:17.033 --> 00:01:18.434
and now you're on summer break.

00:01:18.434 --> 00:01:19.701
-Yeah,
I did not want to do this.

00:01:19.701 --> 00:01:21.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.133 --> 00:01:23.234
It's weird. Like, I love --
I love coming to the show.

00:01:23.234 --> 00:01:25.334
It was always weird
coming back into the building,

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:26.634
though, not...
-Yeah.

00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:29.033
-Like, I almost immediately
pressed the 17th floor

00:01:29.033 --> 00:01:31.000
and all that.
-It is a trip that you --

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.434
Yeah, I mean, 'cause, you know,

00:01:32.434 --> 00:01:34.133
we don't have a summer off
here on this show,

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:37.067
but you can totally
shut your mind off from "SNL."

00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:40.234
-Yeah, it's hard to do,
but I encourage it.

00:01:40.234 --> 00:01:41.367
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:42.801
Although it is very strange

00:01:42.801 --> 00:01:44.901
that you chose to use
your downtime from "SNL"

00:01:44.901 --> 00:01:47.300
to do a second sketch show.
[ Laughs ]

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.701
We've talked about this before.

00:01:48.701 --> 00:01:52.067
I'm so impressed because
I felt like I was just, like --

00:01:52.067 --> 00:01:54.734
there was nothing left of me
after "SNL,"

00:01:54.734 --> 00:01:57.167
and yet you have found time
to do two shows at once.

00:01:57.167 --> 00:01:58.801
-Yeah, it's dumb.
-Yeah.

00:01:58.801 --> 00:02:01.033
-I think, like...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.033 --> 00:02:03.334
I guess it was sold to me
kind of like,

00:02:03.334 --> 00:02:05.300
"Okay, what if you
could do a sketch show

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:07.100
where you can use
the n-word a lot?"

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.200
And I was like,
"That's different enough.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:12.033
I could do that, yeah."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:15.334
-Now, just to make it clear --
in that clip we showed,

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:18.701
that's you basically
having a conference

00:02:18.701 --> 00:02:21.501
with former girlfriends...
-Yeah.

00:02:21.501 --> 00:02:23.501
-...getting notes on what could
make you a better boyfriend.

00:02:23.501 --> 00:02:25.701
-Yeah, my ex-girlfriends
all sit me down

00:02:25.701 --> 00:02:27.501
to give me an intervention,

00:02:27.501 --> 00:02:30.033
but they don't know
that they're my ex-girlfriends.

00:02:30.033 --> 00:02:33.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:34.501
-Now, that's never -- obviously,

00:02:34.501 --> 00:02:35.701
this is not something
in real life

00:02:35.701 --> 00:02:36.868
that you would ever want
to have happen.

00:02:36.868 --> 00:02:40.067
-Nah, it's a fantasy, though.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.067 --> 00:02:41.434
Wouldn't that be cool
to just, like --

00:02:41.434 --> 00:02:43.300
just, like,
get everybody together

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:46.400
and have them kind of all agree
as to why you're horrible?

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:47.567
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:48.934
I would like it on a --

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:51.634
On a person-by-person level,
I would like it.

00:02:51.634 --> 00:02:53.267
I think I would hate them
collectively.

00:02:53.267 --> 00:02:55.300
Like, reaching a consensus
about me, I think,

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.267
would be just devastating.

00:02:57.267 --> 00:02:59.901
-But it would be so fulfilling.
-Yeah.

00:02:59.901 --> 00:03:02.133
-Because now you don't have
to guess anymore.

00:03:02.133 --> 00:03:03.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.033
Like, you know
exactly what's wrong.

00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:07.000
-What percentage of the things
that you're guessing

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:09.501
is wrong about you
do you think you're right about?

00:03:09.501 --> 00:03:10.901
-Well, that's interesting,

00:03:10.901 --> 00:03:14.067
'cause I do think that,
you know, like,

00:03:14.067 --> 00:03:16.901
there are probably a lot
of things that's wrong, like,

00:03:16.901 --> 00:03:20.234
that they would think is right
that's actually not true.

00:03:20.234 --> 00:03:23.467
It's just me being,
I don't know, coy and elusive.

00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:27.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.667 --> 00:03:29.501
But, no, yeah,
I would probably --

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:31.701
I would probably say like 75%.
-Do you think that --

00:03:31.701 --> 00:03:35.067
I wonder if, like,
the criticisms of girlfriends

00:03:35.067 --> 00:03:36.968
that had you at, like,
different parts of your life

00:03:36.968 --> 00:03:38.067
are like massively different

00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:40.133
just based on
where your head was at.

00:03:40.133 --> 00:03:41.501
Or do you think
it's been consistent?

00:03:41.501 --> 00:03:44.367
-I bet it's been consistent.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:46.033
I could hear --
like, you know, sometimes --

00:03:46.033 --> 00:03:47.400
You ever, like --

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.434
You ever, like, get --
go through a breakup

00:03:49.434 --> 00:03:53.300
and you almost hear exactly what
someone else broke up with you?

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:54.300
-Yeah.
-You know what I mean?

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.400
Like, you -- almost verbatim,

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:59.167
somebody broke up with you
for that same exact reason.

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:01.200
And you're like,
"Oh, no, she wasn't lying.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.234
I guess I..."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.234 --> 00:04:05.200
"I think I owe somebody
an apology."

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:06.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.634 --> 00:04:07.834
-Have you -- I've done this.

00:04:07.834 --> 00:04:10.834
I'm -- I don't need to tell
everybody here.

00:04:10.834 --> 00:04:14.334
I'll be driving with my wife
and my three kids in the car,

00:04:14.334 --> 00:04:16.501
and I'll think of, like,
an argument I had with an ex

00:04:16.501 --> 00:04:19.000
where I know I was wrong,
and I'll just go, "Ugh!"

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:20.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.634 --> 00:04:21.767
And my wife will be like,
"What?"

00:04:21.767 --> 00:04:23.968
And I'll be like, "Eh, nothing."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.968 --> 00:04:26.033
-Oh, that's good.
That's...

00:04:26.033 --> 00:04:28.200
I've -- Yeah, that's --
I've definitely had that one.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.601
-Yeah. You --
So, we talked before --

00:04:30.601 --> 00:04:32.133
the first season of
"That Damn Michael Che,"

00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:35.167
you did at the same time you
were doing a season of "SNL."

00:04:35.167 --> 00:04:36.200
-Yeah.

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:38.000
-This year,
was it a little easier

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:40.067
knowing what
you were up against?

00:04:40.067 --> 00:04:42.901
-Yeah, well,
because the first season, like,

00:04:42.901 --> 00:04:45.100
we didn't really know
what the show was.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:46.801
-Mm-hmm.
-And I remember Tina told me

00:04:46.801 --> 00:04:49.734
that, like, I -- I sent like,
Tina some episodes, like,

00:04:49.734 --> 00:04:51.100
"Hey, what did you think
of the show?"

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:52.801
And she was like, "You don't
know what the show is yet,

00:04:52.801 --> 00:04:54.601
but that's okay."
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:54.601 --> 00:04:57.701
And I was infuriated,
'cause she was exactly right.

00:04:57.701 --> 00:04:59.601
Like, after the second season,
I was like,

00:04:59.601 --> 00:05:01.334
"Oh, this is what
she's talking about."

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:03.801
So, like, once you kind of know
what to do with it,

00:05:03.801 --> 00:05:05.400
then you know exactly
how to write it,

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:06.901
and then you can
kind of delegate easier,

00:05:06.901 --> 00:05:08.601
and it's so much easier.

00:05:08.601 --> 00:05:10.033
But it was like -- yeah,

00:05:10.033 --> 00:05:12.334
the first season was way harder
than this one.

00:05:12.334 --> 00:05:14.033
-You have wonderful cameos.

00:05:14.033 --> 00:05:16.067
Obviously, you have a lot
of talented friends.

00:05:16.067 --> 00:05:17.400
-Yeah.
-I think that people think,

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:18.601
when you have talented friends,

00:05:18.601 --> 00:05:21.000
it's easy to ask them
to do your stuff.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:22.868
But it's -- I find it --

00:05:22.868 --> 00:05:25.100
I always feel like they're being
asked a million things,

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:26.267
and i feel bad asking.

00:05:26.267 --> 00:05:28.067
-Yeah, I hate asking people
for stuff,

00:05:28.067 --> 00:05:29.934
'cause especially if it's,
like, my comedy.

00:05:29.934 --> 00:05:31.300
'Cause I know
they're gonna be like,

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:33.167
"Alright, am I gonna have to
read about this tomorrow?"

00:05:33.167 --> 00:05:34.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.868
-You mean that
you're gonna put them

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:37.767
in this sort of jackpot
of getting in trouble?

00:05:37.767 --> 00:05:40.167
-Yeah, like, oh,
maybe I shouldn't say this,

00:05:40.167 --> 00:05:42.667
but I had, like --
we went up to, like,

00:05:42.667 --> 00:05:45.901
Whoopi Goldberg for something,
and she was like, "Absolutely."

00:05:45.901 --> 00:05:47.834
And I couldn't believe she was,
like, willing to do it.

00:05:47.834 --> 00:05:49.200
So I had to tell her,

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:52.067
"Also, in that episode,
we have a Cosby impersonator."

00:05:52.067 --> 00:05:54.133
And she was like,
"No, I can't do it anymore."

00:05:54.133 --> 00:05:55.968
[ Laughter ]

00:05:55.968 --> 00:05:58.634
Like, yeah, I should've probably
started with that one, yeah.

00:05:58.634 --> 00:06:00.567
But, you know,
there's, like, always times

00:06:00.567 --> 00:06:02.133
where, like, people want
to do it, but I'm also like,

00:06:02.133 --> 00:06:04.100
"Man, you got to know
what the whole joke is."

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:05.667
[ Laughter ]
I can't --

00:06:05.667 --> 00:06:07.767
-Yeah, never --
never let Michael Che

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:09.334
sell you on a close-up.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:06:09.334 --> 00:06:10.734
-Like, you definitely want
the wide shot.

00:06:10.734 --> 00:06:12.033
-Yeah, you got to --
you kind of got to know

00:06:12.033 --> 00:06:13.434
what the punchline is.

00:06:13.434 --> 00:06:15.601
It's definitely Bill Cosby
trying to make me a drink.

00:06:15.601 --> 00:06:17.934
[ Laughter ]

00:06:17.934 --> 00:06:19.367
Watch the show --
it makes sense!

00:06:19.367 --> 00:06:20.501
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:20.501 --> 00:06:21.801
No, I --
-In context, it --

00:06:21.801 --> 00:06:23.200
-I think they get it.

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:24.801
Yeah.
-See, a long time ago,

00:06:24.801 --> 00:06:26.167
Bill Cosby
would do this thing --

00:06:26.167 --> 00:06:30.267
No, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:30.267 --> 00:06:32.601
-Now, do you take a break now?
'Cause, obviously,

00:06:32.601 --> 00:06:33.834
you're doing a little bit
of press for the show,

00:06:33.834 --> 00:06:35.000
but it's done.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.267
You got months off for "SNL."

00:06:36.267 --> 00:06:37.234
Are you gonna take a break,

00:06:37.234 --> 00:06:38.534
or are you
one of those workaholics

00:06:38.534 --> 00:06:40.000
who's gonna start doing stand-up
again right away?

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.868
-I'm gonna do stand-up
probably next week, so...

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:43.601
-Yeah.
-Yeah, I just like -- It's --

00:06:43.601 --> 00:06:44.934
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:44.934 --> 00:06:47.801
I think everybody's happy
to hear that.

00:06:47.801 --> 00:06:49.934
-It's always crazy,
because it's like --

00:06:49.934 --> 00:06:53.000
like, my hobbies is my job.
-Yeah.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:55.133
-Like, so, like, any time
I have free time,

00:06:55.133 --> 00:06:56.567
I'm taking a break
from stand-up, that's it,

00:06:56.567 --> 00:06:58.367
and then I'll go somewhere,
and I'm like,

00:06:58.367 --> 00:06:59.567
"Oh, I wonder what
a show would be like in here" --

00:06:59.567 --> 00:07:00.968
you know what I mean?

00:07:00.968 --> 00:07:03.701
And then I end up at a --
doing this bar show in London

00:07:03.701 --> 00:07:04.934
or something or whatever.

00:07:04.934 --> 00:07:07.567
But it's like usually
trying to take a break,

00:07:07.567 --> 00:07:11.501
the first thing I think to relax
is doing stand-up, so it sucks.

00:07:11.501 --> 00:07:13.567
-You seem --
But, like, that makes sense,

00:07:13.567 --> 00:07:17.067
because you have
a very relaxed persona onstage,

00:07:17.067 --> 00:07:19.067
but do you get nervous
when you go do stand-up?

00:07:19.067 --> 00:07:20.601
Like, if you're in London,
you're like,

00:07:20.601 --> 00:07:22.334
"I'm gonna do a set at a bar,"
do you think to yourself --

00:07:22.334 --> 00:07:23.734
as you're driving over,
are you thinking like,

00:07:23.734 --> 00:07:24.901
"Is this going to work here?
Is this...?"

00:07:24.901 --> 00:07:27.067
Or you're mostly
just really excited?

00:07:27.067 --> 00:07:28.567
-No, I don't get nervous,

00:07:28.567 --> 00:07:32.033
because the worst-case scenario
is people don't have fun.

00:07:32.033 --> 00:07:34.601
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:07:34.601 --> 00:07:35.701
[ Laughter ]

00:07:35.701 --> 00:07:38.267
-I mean, honestly,
I hate to say this,

00:07:38.267 --> 00:07:42.567
but it won't ruin my day.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:42.567 --> 00:07:44.133
You know what I mean?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:07:44.133 --> 00:07:47.067
-Like, hey, some shows are
for you, some shows are for me.

00:07:47.067 --> 00:07:49.634
[ Laughter ]
-Well, on behalf of everyone,

00:07:49.634 --> 00:07:51.868
I do want to stress how much
we appreciate your honesty.

00:07:51.868 --> 00:07:53.567
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:53.567 --> 00:07:55.567
-Hey, congrats
on a great second season

00:07:55.567 --> 00:07:56.801
and thank you so much
for being here, buddy.

00:07:56.801 --> 00:07:58.100
-Yeah, thank you, Seth.
-We really appreciate you

00:07:58.100 --> 00:07:59.868
coming back in the building.
-I appreciate it.

00:07:59.868 --> 00:08:01.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
Michael Che, everybody.

00:08:01.133 --> 00:08:02.868
The second season of
"That Damn Michael Che"

00:08:02.868 --> 00:08:04.334
is available now on HBO Max.

00:08:04.334 --> 00:08:05.801
We'll be right back
with Kylie Minogue.

